#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Codex weekly quota reset detector and minimal agent wakeup tool.

Checks Codex subscription rate limits via `codex app-server` stdio JSON-RPC
(`account/read` + `account/rateLimits/read`, zero token usage, no session files
created). Only when the weekly subscription quota window (~10080m / 7d) is
sitting at 100% remaining (0% used) with its 7-day reset clock confirmed to be
drifting unactivated does it send a single minimal, isolated, ephemeral,
read-only `codex exec` request from an empty temporary directory to start the
7-day countdown.

Never hardcodes specific model versions: uses Codex's built-in default model
with low reasoning effort (optional `--model` / `--effort` overrides available).

Compatible with Python 3.8+ (macOS & Linux including Ubuntu 22.04 / WSL2).
"""

